    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341">

                <pb facs="0406" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/13253: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-17T17:00:00+02:00">July 17, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 18—1:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>895. Apropos of the announcement of General Weygand’s appointment as Governor
                    General of Algeria in addition to his other offices, Rochat remarked this
                    afternoon that the appointment was “pleasing to all concerned”: Weygand is given
                    “more direct control thereby in Algeria and Admiral Darlan (as Minister of the
                    Interior) will now have some direct authority over the General.”</p>
                <p>Admiral Abrial,<anchor n="45a" xml:id="d341-f1"/> whose elimination from Algeria
                    did not come as a surprise here, is reputedly slated to be Prefect of the
                    Seine.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leahy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d341-f1" n="45a" xml:id="d341-f1-content">
                <p>Adm. Jean Marie Abrial, former Governor General of Algeria.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
